SUMMARY:Reentrant Algebraic Order at High Temperature
DESCRIPTION:Increasing temperature typically drives systems from order to d
 isorder. This familiar expectation can fail\, however\, when a system is c
 oupled to a critical sector\, a phenomenon often discussed in the context 
 of symmetry non-restoration. In this talk\, I will present a UV-complete m
 odel with a global U(1) symmetry in d = 2 + 1 dimensions that exhibits a B
 erezinskii-Kosterlitz-Thouless (BKT)…\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event
 /17842/
